    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\n`membershipNumber` is a read-only field derived entirely from two already-stored owner fields (`customerCode` and `registrationDate`), so I implemented it as a **derived mapping** \u2014 following the existing precedent of `displayName`/`initials`, which are likewise computed in `OwnerMapper` rather than stored. This avoids an unnecessary entity column, DB migration, and pipeline step.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(... expression = \"java(membershipNumber(owner))\")` plus a small single-responsibility `membershipNumber(Owner)` default method that formats `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'` (`YY` = `registrationDate.getYear() % 100`, zero-padded), returning `null` if either source field is absent.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` and the full suite pass.",
